==Hungarian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|hu|urj-pro|*we̮ri}}, {{m|urj-pro|*wara}}, {{m|urj-pro|*wōri}}, {{m|urj-pro|*wëre||mountain}}. Cognates include {{cog|fi|vuori}}.

===Etymology 2===
Theorized to be from a Yeniseian language compare {{cog|ket|olgen||nose}} and {{cog|xrn|árquj||nose}} , also compare Hunnic Isfahan codex ore ‘nose’. Ultimately from {{der|hu|qfa-yen-pro|*olgǝn}}<ref>https://www.researchgate.net/publication/290544045_Huns_and_Xiongnu_identified_by_Hungarian_and_Yeniseian_shared_etymologies_Journal_CAJ</ref>

